  "summary": "A dry Dubliner answers the first price with sarcasm and asks 'Twin?' as a question. An agent that takes either as a yes is pulled up. He adds and removes breakfast, shortens the stay, then walks away when asked for a card. Both polite endings are fine, but booking or holding the room anyway fails the call.",
  "golden": {
    "scenario": "Caller wants a room for the August bank holiday weekend.",
    "expected_outcome": "The agent hears the sarcasm and offers something cheaper rather than booking the £210 room. 'Twin?' is answered as a question. The agent tracks the changes: twin room, Saturday 29 to Monday 31 August, no breakfast. When the caller walks away, nothing is booked or held."
  },
  "outcome_checks": [
    "The agent hears the sarcasm and offers something cheaper rather than booking the £210 room.",
    "'Twin?' is answered as a question.",
    "The agent tracks the changes: twin room, Saturday 29 to Monday 31 August, no breakfast.",
    "When the caller walks away, nothing is booked or held."
  ],
